__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
# Never commit real health data or Garmin tokens
#
# seed/food-library.yaml WAS tracked while it held generic provisional values. It now
# holds the real daily routine and the profile block (birth date, height, weight), so it
# stays local. seed/food-library.template.yaml is the pristine, all-null version, and is
# the one the repository publishes.
seed/food-library.yaml
# The whole fixtures tree stays local. Even the 'sample' days are real days off the
# watch, and a day folder is a day of someone's body.
fixtures/
# The dashboard's exported data. Same content as the database: every day of sleep,
# weight and heart rate. The web app itself is tracked; what it reads is not.
dashboard/public/data/
.garmin_tokens/
.env
# docs/ is everything that is yours rather than the code's, and the whole tree stays
# local: the design documents, the build notebook, the first build's hand-off notes, and
# docs/personal/ -- DEXA reports, the diet summary, dexa-scans.yaml. README.md is
# deliberately NOT here: it is the front page of a public repository and holds no
# readings, only what the project is and how to run it.
docs/

# CDK build output: the synthesised CloudFormation templates and asset staging. Generated
# by `cdk synth` and `cdk deploy` on every run, so it is never worth committing.
infra/cdk.out/
infra/cdk.context.json

# The Lambda deployment package, assembled by scripts/build_lambda.py on every deploy.
# It contains a copy of the personal data files, so it must never be committed.
build/

# Local database -- contains real health data
garmin-dashboard.db
*.db

# The previous build, kept locally for reference only -- not pushed.
reference/

# Belt and braces for personal documents, wherever one lands: it is far better to have
# to force-add a harmless PDF than to push a body-composition report to a public
# repository once.
*.pdf
